{
  "id": "funnel_pp_additive",
  "reference": "Over-dispersed proportions on a pp funnel: Spiegelhalter 2005 section 5 additive random effects, with the eq. 11 model drawn exactly as a beta-binomial (beta mean = cl, variance = tau^2). phi-hat = 10.854321, tau-hat = 0.098772 on the proportion scale; ucl[0] = 0.667702 at n = 40. In a funnel pp uses this rather than Laney's moving-range sigma_z, which is defined for time order. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
